  "starterCode": "def ml_train_test_split(X: list, y: list, test_size: float = 0.25) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### \ud83d\udca1 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation solves **Train Test Split** directly following its mathematical and algorithmic specification.\n\n### \u26a1 Python Reference Implementation\n```python\ndef ml_train_test_split(X: list, y: list, test_size: float = 0.25) -> dict:\n    n = len(X)\n    n_test = int(round(n * float(test_size)))\n    n_train = n - n_test\n    return {\n        \"X_train\": X[:n_train],\n        \"X_test\": X[n_train:],\n        \"y_train\": y[:n_train],\n        \"y_test\": y[n_train:]\n    }\n```\n\n### \u23f1\ufe0f Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: Optimal for the input dimensions.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary storage.",
